- title: Implement row-independent state streaming
- difficulty_1_to_5: 2
- description: Implement the algebraically simplified kernel with each program independently processing one contiguous V row, computing both FP32 row reductions from one state load before writing the updated row and BF16 output element.
- rationale: The stored K-last layout makes each 128-element row contiguous. Row independence exposes B*8*128 programs, enough parallelism even at B=1, while keeping live state bounded and ensuring the dominant FP32 state is read and written exactly once.

